       "id": "v2-1e331-p64-practice-ae19add4-j2-20261111-root",
       "type": "question",
       "label": null,
       "prompt": "Consider the parabola $y=kx^{2}+2x+k$. Find values of $k$ for which it is always above the $x$-axis.",
       "children": [
        {
         "id": "v2-1e331-p64-practice-ae19add4-j2-20261111-ae19add4-j2-a",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "a",
         "prompt": "State the two conditions, on $k$ and on $\\Delta$, for the parabola to be always above the $x$-axis.",
         "answerSpaceMm": 15,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$k>0$ and $\\Delta<0$",
          "worked": "The parabola must open upwards, so $k>0$.\nIt must have no $x$-intercepts, so $\\Delta<0$."
         }
        },
        {
         "id": "v2-1e331-p64-practice-ae19add4-j2-20261111-ae19add4-j2-b",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "b",
         "prompt": "Find $\\Delta$ in terms of $k$.",
         "answerSpaceMm": 20,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$\\Delta=4-4k^{2}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=2^{2}-4(k)(k)\\\\&=4-4k^{2}\\end{align*}$$"
         }
        },
        {
         "id": "v2-1e331-p64-practice-ae19add4-j2-20261111-ae19add4-j2-c",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "c",
         "prompt": "Solve $\\Delta<0$.",
         "answerSpaceMm": 35,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$k<-1$ or $k>1$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}4-4k^{2}&<0\\\\4(1-k)(1+k)&<0\\end{align*}$$\nThe parabola $y=4-4k^{2}$ opens downwards with intercepts $-1$ and $1$. It is below the axis outside these intercepts.\n$$k<-1\\quad\\text{or}\\quad k>1$$"
         }
        },
        {
         "id": "v2-1e331-p64-practice-ae19add4-j2-20261111-ae19add4-j2-d",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "d",
         "prompt": "Hence find the values of $k$.",
         "answerSpaceMm": 20,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$k>1$",
          "worked": "We need $k>0$ and ($k<-1$ or $k>1$).\nBoth hold only when\n$$k>1$$"
         }
        }
       ],
       "answer": null
